Title: The Lighthouse Wager
Author: Test Fixture
Draft date: 2026-08-22

FADE IN:

EXT. HARBOR TOWN - NIGHT

Rain hammers the cobblestones. A lone figure, MARA (30s, oilskin coat), hurries past shuttered stalls toward the lighthouse on the point.

MARA
(under her breath)
Of all the nights, Tom. Of all the nights.

She pounds on the lighthouse door.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - KEEPER'S ROOM - NIGHT

Cramped, warm, lamplit. TOM GRADY (60s, keeper) opens the door. Wind and rain burst in with Mara.

TOM
You shouldn't be out in this.

MARA
The Peregrine's off the shoals. Nobody's lit the south beacon.

TOM
(beat)
The south beacon's been dark three years, Mara.

MARA
Then tonight it burns.

Tom studies her. Outside, thunder. He grabs his coat.

TOM (CONT'D)
Fetch the oil from the cellar. Go.

CUT TO:

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE - CLIFF PATH - NIGHT

Mara and Tom fight the wind along the cliff path, a lantern swinging between them.

MARA (V.O.)
My father always said the sea takes what it's owed. That night I meant to argue.

FADE OUT.
